Third-party components
----------------------

None. This app has no third-party dependency and no CDN.

Vendored from this project's own kits (same licence, same author), copied verbatim on
25/11/2026:

- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used to write the printable card

Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

What this app is not
--------------------

It is not a crisis service, it cannot tell whether anyone is in danger, and it does not assess risk,
triage, diagnose or give medical advice. It holds a plan the person wrote and shows one grounding
step at a time. It does not replace a crisis line, a clinician, or another person who can be present.

Crisis numbers
--------------

Two numbers ship as a starting point, both labelled in the app as bundled and to be checked for the
person's state: Tele-MANAS on 14416 and the national emergency number 112 (India). The app does not
assert that any number is current or correct, and a number the person types is stored exactly as
typed and marked "as entered by you". If you fork this app for another region, check the numbers
against the official source before shipping them.
